# Testing

- Add tests for important business logic and regressions.
- Prefer behaviour over implementation details; name tests by scenario / expectation / rule.
- Notion reference business cases may inspire tests; they are not automatically unit tests.
- Prefer tests that build the case without bypassing invariants or the model.

## Stack

- xUnit, FluentAssertions, Moq, AutoFixture — via `build/dependencies.props` for `*Tests`.
- Coverage via `.runsettings` (Coverlet) when `CollectCoverage=true`.
- Play’Up web: Vitest / Testing Library — see `playup-web-quality.mdc`.

## TestKit

- Domain / Application situations → **`MyClub.PlayUp.TestKit`** (shared with Development).
- Do not invent a parallel situation kit or pull Infrastructure into TestKit.

## Integration

- `Category=Integration` → Testcontainers PostgreSQL (Docker). Skip locally with `--filter Category!=Integration`.
- Do not point those tests at the Compose `myclub` volume.

## Refactoring

- Understand behaviour and regression risk first; prefer not mixing large refactors with features in one change.
